---
import '../styles/global.css';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const version = '0.1.0-alpha.7';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <meta name="description" content="Dartpollo documentation: generate typed Dart models from GraphQL and execute them with caching, streaming, and cancellation." />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href={`${base}/favicon.svg`} />
    <title>Dartpollo Docs — Typed GraphQL for Dart</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <!--
      DIRECTION: Islands developer manual
      MODE: Read — code and configuration lead; branding stays quiet.
      WORLD: An IDE reference pane using the supplied Islands Dark scheme.
      SIGNATURE: The schema → generated types → client path is expressed as a compact file trace, not a marketing diagram.
      RESPONSIVE: Persistent desktop navigation becomes a horizontal section index on small screens.
    -->
    <a class="skip-link" href="#content">Skip to documentation</a>

    <header class="topbar">
      <a class="brand" href={base} aria-label="Dartpollo documentation home">
        <img src={`${base}/favicon.svg`} alt="" />
        <span>Dartpollo</span>
        <code>{version}</code>
      </a>
      <nav aria-label="External links">
        <a href="https://pub.dev/packages/dartpollo">pub.dev</a>
        <a href="https://github.com/dwikyhardi/dartpollo">GitHub</a>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <div class="page">
      <aside class="sidebar" aria-label="Documentation sections">
        <nav>
          <a href="#overview">Overview</a>
          <a href="#quickstart">Quickstart</a>
          <a href="#packages">Packages</a>
          <a href="#client">Client</a>
          <a href="#caching">Caching</a>
          <a href="#configuration">Generator</a>
        </nav>
        <p>Prerelease API.<br />Expect changes before 1.0.</p>
      </aside>

      <main id="content">
        <section class="intro" id="overview">
          <h1>Typed GraphQL for Dart</h1>
          <p>Dartpollo turns GraphQL schemas and operations into Dart types, then executes them through a client with optional caching, streaming, and cancellation.</p>
          <div class="install" aria-label="Install dartpollo">
            <span>$</span>
            <code>dart pub add dartpollo</code>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="trace" aria-labelledby="trace-title">
          <h2 id="trace-title">How it fits together</h2>
          <ol>
            <li><code>schema.graphql</code><span>API contract</span></li>
            <li><code>query.graphql</code><span>Your operation</span></li>
            <li><code>build_runner</code><span>Generated Dart</span></li>
            <li><code>DartpolloClient</code><span>Typed response</span></li>
          </ol>
        </section>

        <section id="quickstart">
          <h2>Quickstart</h2>
          <p>Add the runtime client and the generator.</p>
          <pre><code>dependencies:
  dartpollo: ^0.1.0-alpha.7

dev_dependencies:
  build_runner: ^2.10.0
  dartpollo_generator: ^0.1.0-alpha.7</code></pre>

          <h3>Map the schema</h3>
          <p>Create <code>build.yaml</code> in the project root.</p>
          <pre><code>targets:
  $default:
    sources:
      - $package$
      - lib/**
      - schema.graphql
    builders:
      dartpollo_generator|dartpollo:
        options:
          schema_mapping:
            - schema: schema.graphql
              queries_glob: lib/**/*.graphql</code></pre>

          <h3>Generate and execute</h3>
          <pre><code>dart run build_runner build --delete-conflicting-outputs</code></pre>
          <pre><code>import 'package:dartpollo/dartpollo.dart';

final client = DartpolloClient(
  'https://api.example.com/graphql',
);

final response = await client.execute(GetUserQuery());
print(response.data);

client.dispose();</code></pre>
        </section>

        <section id="packages">
          <h2>Packages</h2>
          <dl class="packages">
            <div>
              <dt><a href="https://pub.dev/packages/dartpollo">dartpollo</a></dt>
              <dd>Runtime client, typed execution, streaming, cancellation, link composition, and cache stores.</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt><a href="https://pub.dev/packages/dartpollo_generator">dartpollo_generator</a></dt>
              <dd>Build-time generator for operations, response models, inputs, enums, and fragments.</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt><a href="https://pub.dev/packages/dartpollo_annotation">dartpollo_annotation</a></dt>
              <dd>Shared contract between runtime and generator. Most applications receive it transitively.</dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
        </section>

        <section id="client">
          <h2>Client</h2>
          <p>Supply an endpoint and execute generated query objects. Default headers, GET requests, custom Dio clients, request cancellation, and custom <code>gql_link</code> chains are supported.</p>
          <pre><code>final client = DartpolloClient(
  'https://api.example.com/graphql',
  defaultHeaders: &#123;'Authorization': 'Bearer $token'&#125;,
  useGETForQueries: true,
);

final response = await client.execute(
  GetUserQuery(),
  context: Context().withCancelToken(cancelToken),
);</code></pre>
          <p class="note"><strong>Custom transport?</strong> Use <code>DartpolloClient.fromLink</code> with an existing link chain.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="caching">
          <h2>Caching</h2>
          <p>Use <code>DartpolloCachedClient</code> only when the application needs caching. Choose in-memory or Hive persistence, then override policy and TTL per request.</p>
          <pre><code>final client = DartpolloCachedClient(
  'https://api.example.com/graphql',
  cacheStore: InMemoryCacheStore(maxSize: 100),
  defaultCachePolicy: CachePolicy.cacheFirst,
  defaultCacheTtl: Duration(minutes: 5),
);

final response = await client.execute(
  GetUserQuery(),
  context: Context().cacheAndNetwork(),
);</code></pre>
          <table>
            <thead><tr><th>Policy</th><th>Behavior</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td><code>cacheFirst</code></td><td>Use valid cached data; otherwise request the network.</td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>networkFirst</code></td><td>Try the network, then fall back to cache.</td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>cacheOnly</code></td><td>Read locally without a network request.</td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>networkOnly</code></td><td>Skip the cache and fetch fresh data.</td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>cacheAndNetwork</code></td><td>Stream cached data, then the network response.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </section>

        <section id="configuration">
          <h2>Generator configuration</h2>
          <p>Start with defaults. Add options only when the schema needs them.</p>
          <pre><code>options:
  optimize_document_nodes: true
  scalar_mapping:
    - graphql_type: DateTime
      dart_type:
        name: DateTime
    - graphql_type: JSON
      dart_type:
        name: Map&lt;String, dynamic&gt;
  schema_mapping:
    - schema: schema.graphql
      queries_glob: lib/**/*.graphql
      naming_scheme: pathedWithTypes</code></pre>
          <p>Multiple schemas, shared fragment globs, custom scalar imports, enum conversion, naming schemes, and generated-file lint ignores are supported.</p>
          <nav class="next" aria-label="Next resources">
            <a href="https://github.com/dwikyhardi/dartpollo/tree/main/packages/dartpollo/example">Examples</a>
            <a href="https://github.com/dwikyhardi/dartpollo/issues">Issues</a>
          </nav>
        </section>
      </main>
    </div>

    <footer>
      <span>MIT License</span>
      <span>Dartpollo documentation</span>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>
